        {
          "tool_name": "tasks__update",
          "description": "Update an existing automation (scheduled and/or event-triggered). Use this only when the user asks to change, edit, or modify an existing automation's name, prompt, schedule, event trigger filters, or notification settings. This is a patch: send only the fields that change (`task_id` is required; `name` and `prompt` are optional). Do not call this in the same turn as automation_create to finish a just-created automation — put the complete args in one create. Requires `task_id` from `automation_list`. When adding or changing an event trigger, or when the updated prompt starts using a third-party service (Gmail, Outlook, Slack, Notion, Linear, GitHub, calendar, finance, …), first call `search_connected_tools` with that service name. A valid connection exists only when results include tools whose `remote_name` is that service — not Automations tools that merely mention it. If none appear, call `request_connector_auth` and do not update until the user connects. Webhook needs no connector. Include `schedule_id` when changing a schedule; include `trigger` when changing event filters (call automation_list_trigger_catalog for allowed providers/types/dimensions; for GitHub repos prefer numeric ids from automation_list_trigger_resources — owner/name is resolved when unique; for Linear teams / projects / authors prefer UUIDs or `me`; display names are resolved when unique). Omitting `trigger` leaves existing event triggers unchanged.",
